<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georg Philipp Telemann</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1681–<a href="/years/1767">1767</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Georg Philipp Telemann was a German composer and one of the most prolific of all time. After posts at Sorau and as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapellmeister">Kapellmeister</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisenach">Eisenach</a> court from 1708, he worked in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> and from 1721 until his death as director of music for the five main churches of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a>. He wrote operas, cantatas, passions and much instrumental music, and was godfather to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carl-philipp-emanuel-bach">Carl Philipp Emanuel Bach</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/georg-philipp-telemann.jpg" alt="Georg Philipp Telemann" width="320" height="466" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Valentin Daniel Preisler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Telemann.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
